Package: fleet
Title: Mean-Field Twin of the 'malariasimulation' Malaria Model
Version: 0.0.0.9003
Authors@R: c(
  person("Peter", "Winskill", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), email = "p.winskill@imperial.ac.uk"))
Description: Provides a fast, deterministic mean-field counterpart to the
  'malariasimulation' individual-based model of Plasmodium falciparum and
  Plasmodium vivax malaria, advanced one day at a time on the individual-based
  model's own daily clock. The human population is structured by age and biting
  heterogeneity, and for vivax by hypnozoite batch, with the full acquired- and
  maternal-immunity model, coupled to a compartmental larval-and-adult
  mosquito model and driven by the same intervention modules:
  clinical treatment and antimalarial resistance, bed nets and indoor residual
  spraying, chemoprevention (MDA, SMC, PMC), pre-erythrocytic and
  transmission-blocking vaccines, seasonality, and custom demography. It
  accepts an unmodified 'malariasimulation' parameter list, is seeded at the
  'malariaEquilibrium' or 'malariaEquilibriumVivax' solution, and returns
  'malariasimulation'-style outputs that feed directly into 'postie'. Built on
  the 'odin2' and 'dust2' stack, a multi-decade falciparum run completes in
  about two seconds, independent of population size.
